cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  For released material, cite Medicine and Health Sciences Foundational Branch
  Paper 001 through its current DOI lineage, and cite each other released branch
  through its own immutable DOI. The Lean-verified 2 August 2026 successor suite
  is published. Status-corrected patch versions remove the erroneous
  prepublication wording while preserving all scientific content; the current
  Lean citation record is publications/lean4_verification/CITATION.cff.
title: "Ernos Labs Smithian Fold Theory Open Science Platform and Knowledge Tree"
type: software
version: 3.0.0-medicine-foundation-paper-001-v1.0
date-released: 2026-07-27
authors:
  - family-names: Smith
    given-names: Maria
    email: Maria.Smith.Sftoe@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/MettaMazza/ernos-labs-sft-platform"
url: "https://github.com/MettaMazza/ernos-labs-sft-platform"
abstract: >-
  Accessible Python clean-room reconstruction of Smithian Fold Theory with one
  fail-closed admission engine, exact candidate enumeration, unique-survivor
  forcing, adverse controls, independent reconstruction, sealed empirical
  comparison and immutable receipts. The Medicine and Health Sciences
  foundation contains 72 engine-admitted laws from 18,432 enumerated
  candidates, 288 passing adverse controls, 72 independent reconstructions and
  72 post-seal comparisons. Its V1/V2 audit reviews all 763 prior entries and
  closes all five Medicine-owned atoms at explicit clinical evidence boundaries.
keywords:
  - Smithian Fold Theory
  - exact arithmetic
  - computational proof
  - empirical validation
  - clean-room reconstruction
  - open science
  - reproducibility
license: Apache-2.0
